# Version Management

## Single Source of Truth

The Jarvis application version lives in one place: `VERSION` (project root).
All services read from `lib/version.py` or the VERSION file directly at runtime.

## NEVER Do This

- NEVER manually edit version strings in code files (api/__init__.py, server.py, health.py, etc.)
- NEVER manually edit the version in README.md or docs/README.md footers
- NEVER hardcode a version like `"2.40.0"` in Python files - always import from `lib/version.py`
- NEVER update pyproject.toml version manually

## How to Change the Version

Use the bump script:
```bash
./bin/bump-version patch    # 2.40.0 -> 2.40.1
./bin/bump-version minor    # 2.40.0 -> 2.41.0
./bin/bump-version major    # 2.40.0 -> 3.0.0
./bin/bump-version 2.50.0   # Set explicit version
./bin/bump-version           # Sync all files to current VERSION (no change)
```

The script updates: VERSION file, pyproject.toml, README.md footer, docs/README.md footer.
All Python services read VERSION at runtime so they pick up changes on restart.

## What Reads VERSION at Runtime

- `lib/version.py` -> exports `JARVIS_VERSION`
- api/__init__.py, api/server.py, api/routes/health.py
- jarvis-web/server/routes/api.py, jarvis-web/server/app.py (startup banner)
- jarvis-canvas/__init__.py, jarvis-canvas/server/routes/health.py
- jarvis-memory/server/app.py, jarvis-intelligence/server/app.py
- bin/jarvis-dashboard (TUI status bar)
- bin/wake_jarvis.py, bin/wake_jarvis_local.py (startup output)

## Independent Versions (Do NOT Centralize)

These have their own versioning and should NOT be tied to JARVIS_VERSION:
- Workflow schema versions (data/workflows/*.json)
- Tool versions in *.tool.json (managed by evolution system)
- Config format versions (status_phrases.json, etc.)
- Individual doc page revisions
- External API versions
